> = What kind of encrypted communication does Linux offer? =
> 
> Linux offers several programs that can aid in encrypting communications. Most notably, a Linux version of the [http://www.gnupg.org Gnu Privacy Guard] (GPG), an open source version of the more-famous PGP (Pretty Good Privacy) is available from the [http://www.fsf.org/ Free Software Foundation]. Additionally, there are [http://gaim.sourceforge.net/plugins.php plugins] for the instant messaging client [http://gaim.sourceforge.net/ Gaim] that allow the user to send IMs with RSA or GPG encryption.
